  The other day at lunch, discussion drifted from normal Nethack
smalltalk onto Calvin and Hobbes.  Somebody mentioned Calvin's
transmogrifer [sic] and almost as per reflex somebody else mumbled
"You see here a large box".  This evolved quite naturally into Yet
Another Nethack Item idea: a large box, that's actually a
transmogrifer, i.e.  a polymorphing device.  Here's a sketch for the
behaviour:

  o	1/25 chance of a large box being a transmogrifer.  The box
	should appear as "a large box" until identified as a
	"transmogrifer".

  o	An item put into the box will be polymorphed at once.  You will
	notice this when examining the box (BTW, nice ":"-command here
	in 3.1) or looting it.

  o	Each box has 1-8 charges.  Polypiling 8 items with a WoP is
	normally "safe" and a WoP usually has several charges, so
	this does not seem like too many.

  o	I'm not quite sure what the effect of putting a tiger corpse
	into it should be, but it would seem appropriate that such an
	action made the tiger come back to life as your pet.  If you
	are a tiger yourself something else could also happen.

  o	There should never be any litterature (spellbooks, scrolls)
	inside a transmogrifer.  Rather, there should be a higher
	chance of finding any of these very Calvin'ish items:
		- ring of conflict
		- rubber hose
		- candy bar
		- cream pie
		- pancake
		- hallucination
		- drum of earthquake
		- blindfold (tribute to Spaceman Spiff)

  Now, I know Calvin and Hobbes has nothing to do with AD&D, but they
have quite a lot of fans among computer-users; a list of "most popular
machine name on the Internet" I saw a year ago had the name "calvin"
(Or was it "hobbes"?  Anyway, they were both up there) in the top-5,
for instance.
  BTW, there's still room for additional ideas; cursed/uncursed/blessed
status, kicking it while hallucinating ("You suddenly yearn for a
tunafish sandwich."), etc etc.

  ciao, Peter


